course: dictionary
lesson: 15807
title: Words that mean very strong
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word unbreakable is made of three parts: un- means not, break means to split or snap, and -able means can be done. So unbreakable means cannot be broken, or is so strong it is very hard to break. «The toddler's beaker is unbreakable, so it can fall on the kitchen floor.» The beaker will not crack when it drops.
explain: The word can also describe things that are not solid, like a promise or a bond. «Mia and Sam made an unbreakable promise to always be friends.» Here it means the promise is too strong to be ended or broken.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «could not be broken» in place of unbreakable. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right. In real life nothing is truly unbreakable, so the word means very, very strong.
fact: Unbreakable means very hard or impossible to break.
fact: «Unbreakable» can describe objects, like «unbreakable plastic» or «unbreakable toys».
fact: «Unbreakable» can also describe promises, bonds, rules and codes that cannot be ended or beaten.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so «unbreakable» means not able to be broken.
fact: In science, nothing is truly unbreakable; the word means very strong.
exercise: «The toddler's beaker is made of unbreakable plastic.» What does unbreakable mean here? | Sharp and shiny | Easy to bend | * Very hard to break | Full of water
exercise: «Their friendship was an unbreakable bond.» Find and copy the one word that shows the bond was very strong. | * unbreakable | bond | friendship | their
exercise: The word «unbreakable» has three parts: un-, break and -able. What does the part un- mean? | very big | again | before | * not
test: «The king's rule was unbreakable: nobody could change it.» What does unbreakable suggest? | Quite funny | Made of glass | * Too strong to be changed or ended | Very quiet
test: Ella says, «This code is unbreakable.» Why might she say that? | It is already broken | * It is too strong for anyone to crack | It is made of soft cloth | It is written in pencil
exam: What does unbreakable mean in «an unbreakable record»? | * So strong that nobody has ever beaten it | Full of holes | Easy to read aloud | Very small and light
